  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Ronan Farrow is a prominent investigative journalist and New Yorker contributing writer known for exposing Harvey Weinstein’s sexual misconduct, which propelled the #MeToo movement. After leaving NBC News in 2017—claiming they stifled his reporting—he released the best-selling book and podcast Catch and Kill. Currently, he produces HBO documentaries and covers major corporate/political power abuses. Key Details on His Career and Recent Work: Investigative Impact: Farrow won a Pulitzer Prize in 2018 for his reporting in The New Yorker on Weinstein and subsequent investigations into other high-profile abuse cases. Conflict with NBC: Farrow documented in Catch and Kill that NBC executives blocked his reporting on Weinstein. He alleged the network was protecting its own reputation and anchor Matt Lauer, a claim NBC has contested. Current Projects: As of 2026, he continues to produce high-stakes journalism, recently investigating OpenAI CEO Sam Altman and the AI industry. Documentary Work: Farrow has created several HBO documentaries, including Surveilled (2024) and Endangered (2022). Personal Life: Farrow was previously engaged to Jon Lovett, but the pair separated in 2023.",
